    "original_text": "ASTIS exact scoped domain background / source consumer restatement:\nReal complete second-countable normed vector space E with Borel measurable structure, Gaussian probability measure mu (possibly noncentered/degenerate).\nActual globally Lipschitz scalar function f:E->R with NNReal constant L, including L=0. No differentiability, boundedness, positive dimension, given mean, Laplace certificate or sharp coefficient premise.\nFor every actual Gaussian mu and globally L-Lipschitz scalar f on the stated Banach/Borel space, f is Bochner integrable and exp(t*(f-int f dmu)) is integrable for every real t. This is a Gaussian-domain background theorem, not the sharp concentration bound.\nGenuine Gaussian-gradient-output first Bochner moment and every signed directional centered exponential L1, plus existing exact positive-step proximal/input/noise semantics only. Sharp centered coefficient eta*normu^2/2 in4.3, bias4.2, FIRSTW2/LSI/T2/fullLemma4.2, posterior jointkernel/higher smoothing/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization/main/work/composition remainOPEN. Domain proof is authored Fernique alternative, not Gaussian concentration constant. TV never transfers unboundedcost. Exactstatements/topology alreadysealed beforeproof; no unreviewed signature gap.",
    "text_sha256": "0897c4cb35525e6337406bfddbe51bb91f768e6b0f156dcb715e0b59f9db1940"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianLipschitzExponential.integrable_and_integrable_exp_centered_of_lipschitz",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Probability/GaussianLipschitzExponential.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E} [ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian μ]\n    {L : ℝ≥0} {f : E → ℝ} (hf : LipschitzWith L f) :\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable f μ ∧ ∀ t : ℝ,\n      MeasureTheory.Integrable\n        (fun x => Real.exp (t * (f x - ∫ z, f z ∂μ))) μ",
    "statement_sha256": "386f8e0c54839adabeae5d0334fec161335e5940f61599a6df71831f8282002a",
