  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be any real normed vector space whose additive group is a normed additive commutative group, with a complete norm topology, a second-countable topology, and a measurable structure equal to its Borel structure. Let mu be any Gaussian probability measure on E, in the sense that every continuous real linear functional has a Gaussian pushforward; its mean is unrestricted and degeneracy is allowed. Let L be any nonnegative real Lipschitz constant, including L = 0, and let f: E -> R satisfy the global bound |f(x) - f(y)| <= L ||x - y|| for all x,y in E. Then f is Bochner integrable with respect to mu, and for every real t, including negative t and t = 0, the function x |-> exp(t (f(x) - m)), where m = integral_E f(z) dmu(z) is the actual mean of f under mu, is Bochner integrable with respect to mu. The conclusion is integrability of each such centered exponential; it supplies no quantitative bound on its integral.",
    "text_sha256": "8365924dabad832e7ceedef6e6a986ebd31af5c45902444c1fb247480cfe091d",
    "decoder": "blind_statement_decoder_29",
